                  {
                      "parameters":  {
                                         "content":  "## 🚨 [Ops] Error Handler → Slack\n\n**Reusable error notifier for your whole n8n instance.**\n\nWhenever a workflow that points to this one fails, n8n triggers it\nautomatically and posts the failure details to Slack:\nworkflow name, the node that failed, the error message, and a link\nto the failed execution.\n\n### How to attach it to a workflow\nOpen any workflow → **Settings (3 dots) → Settings → Error Workflow**\n→ select **[Ops] Error Handler → Slack**.\n\n### Setup\n- Pick your Slack credential + alert channel on the **Send Slack Alert** node.\n- That\u0027s it — no trigger to run manually; it fires on failures.",
                                         "height":  300,
                                         "width":  560,
                                         "color":  2
                                     },
                      "type":  "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
                      "typeVersion":  1,
                      "position":  [
                                       -360,
                                       -360
                                   ],
                      "id":  "sticky-err-overview",
                      "name":  "Sticky Error Overview"
                  },
                  {
                      "parameters":  {

                                     },
                      "type":  "n8n-nodes-base.errorTrigger",
                      "typeVersion":  1,
                      "position":  [
                                       -300,
                                       0
                                   ],
                      "id":  "err-trigger-0001",
                      "name":  "On Error",
                      "notes":  "Fires automatically when any workflow that has this set as its Error Workflow fails. Receives the failed execution + error details."
                  },
                  {
                      "parameters":  {
                                         "jsCode":  "// Build a readable Slack alert from the Error Trigger payload\nconst d = $json || {};\nconst e = d.execution || {};\nconst w = d.workflow || {};\nconst err = e.error || {};\n\nconst text = [\n  \u0027\\uD83D\\uDD34 *n8n workflow FAILED*\u0027,\n  `*Workflow:* ${w.name || \u0027unknown\u0027}  (${w.id || \u0027-\u0027})`,\n  `*Failed at node:* ${e.lastNodeExecuted || \u0027unknown\u0027}`,\n  `*Mode:* ${e.mode || \u0027-\u0027}`,\n  `*Error:* ${err.message || \u0027no message\u0027}`,\n  e.url ? `*Open execution:* ${e.url}` : \u0027\u0027\n].filter(Boolean).join(\u0027\\n\u0027);\n\nreturn [{ json: { text } }];\n"
                                     },
                      "type":  "n8n-nodes-base.code",
                      "typeVersion":  2,
                      "position":  [
                                       -100,
                                       0
                                   ],
                      "id":  "err-format-0002",
                      "name":  "Format Error Message",
                      "notes":  "Turns the raw error payload into a readable Slack message."
                  },
                  {
                      "parameters":  {
                                         "resource":  "message",
                                         "operation":  "post",
                                         "select":  "channel",
                                         "channelId":  {
                                                           "__rl":  true,
                                                           "value":  "C0BCDBS0WNA",
                                                           "mode":  "id",
                                                           "cachedResultName":  "all-slack-automation"
                                                       },
                                         "text":  "={{ $json.text }}",
                                         "otherOptions":  {

                                                          }
                                     },
                      "type":  "n8n-nodes-base.slack",
                      "typeVersion":  2.3,
